# Page vs Presentation

## Pages (`**/Page.tsx`)

- Orchestrate only: route params, fetch/load, context/hooks, toasts, navigation, composition.
- Export `Page`; re-export via domain barrel (`Orders.Index`, `Menu.Show`).
- Do not embed large tables, dialogs, or card markup — extract presentation.

## Presentation

| Layer | Where | When |
|-------|--------|------|
| Global | `components/atoms\|molecules\|organisms` | Used across domains |
| Domain | `pages/**/<domain>/shared/` | Used by 2+ screens in that domain |
| Page-local | Sibling of `Page.tsx` | Used by that screen only |

Promote only when a second consumer appears. Props in, callbacks out — no fetches in presentation.

## Folder shape

```
pages/dashboard/orders/
  Orders.tsx
  shared/OrderCard.tsx
  index/Page.tsx
  new/Page.tsx
  show/Page.tsx
```

`Routes.tsx` imports barrels, not deep paths. Dashboard shell (`Dashboard`, `Sidebar`) is layout, not a domain Page.

## Also

- Spanish UI copy in existing Spanish flows.
- Call `services/*` / context from Pages — not Axios from components when a service exists.
- Prefer `useForm` / `useCart`; no one-off “useThisPage” god hooks.

